What this licence covers, and what it does not.

Covers: the project's own source, tools, tests, build scripts and
documentation -- everything in this repository that the project authored,
unless a file or directory says otherwise. Third-party components keep their
own licences; see THIRD-PARTY.md.

Does not cover:

  * Tokimeki Memorial: Forever with You. The game, its code, its data, its
    art, its music and its text are (c) Konami. This repository holds no disc
    images and none of the game's data files, Japanese script text, art,
    audio or video. It does contain an unofficial English translation of the
    game's script (translation/, config/patch/) and English lettering drawn
    for the game's pictures (src/patch/art/), which are a fan translation:
    the MIT grant covers only the translators' and artists' own work, and
    grants no right in the underlying work.
    The patched disc is built on your machine from your own copy (README.md);
    the patch code (src/patch/) runs inside the game and calls its functions
    by address. The MIT grant covers only the project's own expression in
    these. It grants no right in the game, and the project claims none.
  * Trademarks. "Tokimeki Memorial" is a trademark of Konami; "PlayStation"
    is a trademark of Sony Interactive Entertainment. This is an unofficial
    fan project, not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Konami or
    Sony. Neither this licence nor the project grants any trademark right.
  * The decompilation the patch builds against (toki1-decomp) and the PC port
    (toki1-pc) are separate repositories with their own licences.
  * The vendored third-party files listed in THIRD-PARTY.md, which carry
    their own terms.
